{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QGaussianBinomialPascal","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QGaussianBinomialPascal","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.rogersSzego_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.rogersSzego_two","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QGaussianBinomialPascal.lean#L86-L98","doc":"`H_2(t;q) = 1 + [2]_q·t + t²` with `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹` (balanced). The middle coefficient is\nthe balanced quantum integer — the first place balanced vs standard normalization differ\n(`q+q⁻¹` here, `1+q` for the standard `(q;q)` Rogers–Szegő). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.rogersSzego_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.rogersSzego_one","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QGaussianBinomialPascal.lean#L79-L84","doc":"`H_1(t;q) = 1 + t` (the `n=1` binomials are both `1` in any normalization, so this is the\nboundary value the even/odd-vanishing argument needs — at `t=−1`, `H_1 = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.rogersSzego_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.rogersSzego_zero","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QGaussianBinomialPascal.lean#L75-L77","doc":"`H_0(t;q) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.rogersSzego","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.rogersSzego","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QGaussianBinomialPascal.lean#L68-L73","doc":"The **(balanced) Rogers–Szegő polynomial** value\n`H_n(t;q) = Σ_{k=0}^n [n choose k]_q · tᵏ`, in the balanced `qBinom`. The q-oscillator /\ncontinuous q-Hermite generating polynomial (balanced normalization — see the file's\nnormalization caveat). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_pascal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.QPartitionCombinatorics.qBinom_pascal","kind":"theorem","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/QGaussianBinomialPascal.lean#L29-L64","doc":"**q-Pascal rule** for the Gaussian binomial (`q > 1`, `m`-parametrised, `n = k+1+m`):\n`[k+m+2 choose k+1]_q = q^{m+1}·[k+1+m choose k]_q + q^{-(k+1)}·[k+1+m choose k+1]_q`.\nDerived from `qBracket_add` via the `qFactorial` ratio — the recurrence behind the\nRogers–Szegő / continuous q-Hermite three-term relation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}